From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rahanahu <rahanahu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vasio: remove only the peer's own entry from the name table

The registry gives a connecting peer the name from its announcement
(SetInfo()) before it checks whether the name is in use. When it refuses
the peer because another participant has that name, the refused peer
carries the same name, and when its connection ends,
RemovePeerFromConnection() erases the name from _participantNameToPeer
without looking at which peer the entry belongs to. The entry of the
participant that has the name is gone: the registry ignores the
RemoteParticipantConnectRequest of a participant that joins afterwards
and can reach that participant only through the registry ("Ignoring
invalid RemoteParticipantConnectRequest"), and the join times out
waiting for its reply. The registry's proxy uses the same table.

Erase the entry only if it maps to the peer that is removed.
AssociateParticipantNameAndPeer() already keeps an existing entry
(insert()), so the refused peer never had one of its own.
---
 SilKit/source/core/vasio/VAsioConnection.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/SilKit/source/core/vasio/VAsioConnection.cpp b/SilKit/source/core/vasio/VAsioConnection.cpp
index b99147d..ec0ab8e 100644
--- a/SilKit/source/core/vasio/VAsioConnection.cpp
+++ b/SilKit/source/core/vasio/VAsioConnection.cpp
@@ -1441,7 +1441,13 @@ void VAsioConnection::RemovePeerFromConnection(IVAsioPeer* peer)
         auto simulationIt{_participantNameToPeer.find(peer->GetSimulationName())};
         if (simulationIt != _participantNameToPeer.end())
         {
-            simulationIt->second.erase(peer->GetInfo().participantName);
+            // Only the peer's own entry: a peer that was refused because another one has its
+            // name carries that name too, and must not remove the other one's entry.
+            auto participantIt{simulationIt->second.find(peer->GetInfo().participantName)};
+            if (participantIt != simulationIt->second.end() && participantIt->second == peer)
+            {
+                simulationIt->second.erase(participantIt);
+            }
         }
     }
 
